      "content": "it doesnt feel like \"pushing boundaries\" though... it feels like a wall. like my brain is being muted. i was reading some stuff online about how certain companies use sub-audible hertz to stabilize user attention, and i'm starting to think they're doing it to stop people from thinking outside the box. is there any way to test if there's an actual frequency coming from them? like, how could i build something to block it out?",
